  Where the brief's diagnosis didn't hold

  - B (DEG/EG): the Instructions filter alone wasn't enough. DEG/EG's header finder picks the first data row, because its "Active ingredient" matches the
    hint ingredient and the merged real header has fewer filled cells. So Function values became material names even on a single-sheet upload. As you chose,
    the template is now read through docgen_template.deg_eg_sheet and fed to DEG/EG's own parser. This only happens when the header spans more than one
    row, so a flat sheet named "OSD" keeps today's reader and its Material Code column.
  - C1 (Talc): "Talc" already matched IMI Fabi Talc 140 USP-EP-ChP, because compendial suffixes were already stripped. The real failure is that the page
    prompt lists the product's name from every page. The letterhead name and the table header "Mineral / Talc 140…" then become two materials, one of them
    empty, and matching fails with "Multiple compatible annexures exist for material family 'talc'". I reproduced this through the real converter on an
    11-page reconstruction; it fails on the original code and passes now. The fix: scope merging ignores the document's own supplier name and compendial
    tags, and a "Not tested" row can't overwrite a real reading. The other C1 mechanisms (grade-number tolerance, stated-grade match, letter/digit
    splitting) already existed; I only added tests for them. C2's per-page names were already being added as candidates.
  - A2: a pre-existing bug. The q.s. Water-for-Injection row made an empty Qty/mL column look filled, so every amount came out blank. The basis now requires
    an actual number.

